      "body": "# **TL;DR:**\n\nEmergent is the best vibe coding tool for transforming your ideas into fully functional, production-ready apps. No developers are required.\n\n# **🚀 Introducing Emergent 🚀**\n\nEmergent is your on-demand CTO and founding engineer, reinventing product development. Our state-of-the-art (SOTA) coding agents deliver production-ready, full-stack applications with stunning UI and real backend, transforming ideas into market-ready products. No developers are required.\n\nWe go beyond just prototypes and mockups. Emergent ships fully functional apps with real backend, databases, and integrations -- built and deployed without ever leaving the platform.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/lT2dRng4fc0\n\n### **😖 The Problem:**\n\nShipping products is hard for non-technical builders, due to expensive engineering talent, inflexible no-code platforms, or AI tools that produce half-baked prototypes. As a result, most ideas never make it past the whiteboard or overcome the barriers to real-world execution.\n\n### **🤓 Our Solution:**\n\nEmergent redefines how a product gets built. At its core, Emergent is more than a coding assistant. It's a fully integrated platform that autonomously builds, tests, and ships software. What Emergent stands for: \n\n* Conversation-to-code transformation: Describe your product in plain language — Emergent handles architecture, logic, and implementation.\n* Fully Autonomous End-to-End Development: Our agents plan, build, test, and debug apps fully autonomously to produce shippable apps.\n* Built-in deployment: Ship fast and learn faster. Emergent manages the entire product lifecycle, from concept to customers.\n\n### **👷🏽 Why We're Building This**\n\nEmergent aims to democratize access to advanced software creation, empowering new builders to turn their visions into reality without traditional barriers. We’ve watched great ideas get stuck on whiteboards because building them was too hard, expensive, or slow. As engineers and builders, we saw that AI could change this by writing code, truly understanding what’s needed, and building complete solutions.\n\n![uploaded image](/media/?type=post&id=90629&key=user_uploads/529149/9ae44e4c-78fd-4811-9566-0f53818ded4c)\n\n### **🥷🏼 Emergent In Action**\n\nJust two weeks after our alpha launch, users built over 10,000 apps on Emergent. These range from simple, elegant landing pages to complex SaaS tools like AI notetakers, Slack bots, and Figma plugins — endless possibilities.\n\nHere are some apps built by our users:\n\n* https://youtu.be/coGyUTUrpJY\n* https://youtu.be/yXdk_feMJ4E\n* https://youtu.be/etipqXln6zY\n\n_Please note: Emergent is still invite-only, but we’ll be launching to the public soon. Want early access? Use code: #**EMERGENTFORYC**_\n\n### **🦄 Team**\n\nEmergent was founded by twin brothers **Mukund Jha (CEO)** and **Madhav Jha (CTO)**, who are dedicated to democratizing product development and making it more accessible.\n\n* Mukund was previously Co-Founder/CTO at Dunzo -- India's first quick commerce offering (backed by Google and Reliance). He is a graduate of Columbia Engineering and has experience working at Google.\n* Madhav got his PhD in Theoretical Computer Science from Penn State University and was a von Neumann postdoctoral fellow at Sandia National Labs. He was the founding member of the research team that built and shipped Amazon Sagemaker.\n\nOutside of work, the Jha brothers enjoy spending time with family and friends in both San Francisco and Bengaluru.\n\n![uploaded image](/media/?type=post&id=90629&key=user_uploads/529149/7a9a91b8-2795-4fb5-87a5-14fc77d238c3)\n\nxoxo\n\nTeam Emergent 🫡\n\n![uploaded image](/media/?type=post&id=90629&key=user_uploads/529149/7f26b476-30f1-47f5-bbe1-b042c03c58a5)\n\n",
